# Python Project — simple script with tests
#
# This example shows:
#   - Running pytest via shell commands
#   - Using the LLM to explain test failures
#   - Task arguments (justprompt test mymodule)
#
# Try it:
#   justprompt --list              # see available tasks
#   justprompt --dry-run test      # preview what would happen
#   justprompt test                # run tests + get LLM analysis

llm claude [model=sonnet]

# Run tests and ask the LLM to analyze any failures
task test:
    !python -m pytest app_test.py -v 2>&1 || true
    Look at the test output above.
    If all tests passed, just say "All tests passed" and nothing else.
    If any tests failed, explain the root cause of each failure
    and suggest a concrete fix.

# Generate a docstring for a module
task document(module):
    !cat {{module}}.py
    Read the Python code above and generate clear Google-style
    docstrings for every public function and class.
    Output the complete file with docstrings added.

# Lint and suggest improvements
task review:
    !find . -name "*.py" -not -path "./.venv/*" | head -5
    !cat app.py
    Review this Python code for:
    - bugs or edge cases
    - style issues (PEP 8)
    - possible simplifications
    Be concise. Only mention real issues.
